@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title PLANNED — Operate sbx on a cloud host over SSH

node "Operator workstation" {
  component "Proveo UI\nOpenSSH client" as CLIENT
}
node "Operator-controlled Ubuntu cloud host" {
  component "Proveo runner\nsbx CLI and daemon" as RUNNER
  database "Remote Git checkout\nor staged worktree" as WORK
  database "Remote sbx credential store\nand egress policy" as STATE
  node "sbx microVM\ncoding agent and tools" as VM
}
cloud "Git remote and\nmodel providers" as NET

CLIENT ARROW_MAIN RUNNER : SSH and terminal I/O
RUNNER ARROW_MAIN VM : create, attach, stop, remove
WORK ARROW_MAIN VM : remote-host workspace or clone
STATE ARROW_MAIN VM : brokered access
VM ARROW_MAIN NET : remote-host egress policy

note bottom of CLIENT
  The OS picker previews this path when the cursor
  rests on the disabled cloud option. The grid fits
  the short name. Its hint says coming soon.
end note

note bottom of RUNNER
  First validate one supported Ubuntu host with
  working KVM and the installed Proveo/sbx versions.
  A cloud bare-metal host is the initial candidate.
  A nested-KVM VM is a second candidate once
  sbx diagnose and a real create/run pass there.
  Run the whole Proveo backend on that host first.
  Reuse its config, receipt and cleanup behavior.
end note

legend bottom
  **Initial use case**
  Run a long build or coding session from a laptop while compute, checkout, artifacts
  and the policy/credential store stay on an operator-controlled machine. Start with
  an existing remote Git checkout and an interactive SSH PTY. Return results through
  Git or explicit artifact transfer. Keep credential enrollment on the remote host.
  A later local picker can target a configured OpenSSH host and hand execution to a
  version-matched remote Proveo. Decide how to stage local dirty files before exposing
  the mode. Evaluate local-device forwarding independently of the initial remote run.

  **Verification before enabling the option**
  Run sbx diagnose and create a Proveo kit sandbox on the target host. Verify workspace
  scope, policy, agent launch via PTY, reconnect, no loss of uncommitted work on cleanup,
  and return of Git refs and an artifact. Measure nested KVM separately if using it.
  For editor access, try the remote host's sbx SSH proxy after the core run is proven.

  **Evidence**
  * Docker local install and KVM requirements
    https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/install/
  * Local workspace paths and host-side networking
    https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/architecture/
  * Docker-managed sbx --cloud uses its own API, store and workspace model
    https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/cloud/local-vs-cloud/
  * Built-in sbx SSH uses a daemon socket on the machine that runs sbx
    https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/integrations/#how-ssh-connections-work
  * Community report using SSH to run the remote host's sbx SSH proxy
    https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/issues/523
  * Open nested-KVM request on Docker's issue tracker
    https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/issues/425
  * EC2 and Compute Engine document nested virtualization on supported instances
    https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/amazon-ec2-nested-virtualization.html
    https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/nested-virtualization/overview
endlegend
@enduml
